From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:30:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable gecko-gated properties and values in the servo build

Each of these was gated to the gecko engine although nothing
gecko-specific backs it. Dropping the gate lets the servo build parse
and compute it.

accent-color: the embedder's form-control paint (checkbox, radio, range)
reads it to colour the widgets like real browsers, instead of falling
back to the element's text colour.

appearance: the Appearance value type was already un-gated, and the
existing extra_prefixes line gives the -webkit-appearance legacy alias,
which is the spelling stylesheets use for form-control resets. This is
parse and computed value only; appearance:none does not suppress widget
chrome in paint.

break-before, break-after, break-inside and box-decoration-break: print
stylesheets set break-inside:avoid on nearly every table and figure, and
without the parse a PDF pipeline can never honour them. Fragmentation
itself is not implemented here.

-webkit-text-fill-color: overlay code editors (a transparent textarea
stacked on a highlighted <pre>) hide the textarea's glyphs with
-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent and keep the caret visible with
caret-color. The longhand was fully defined but gated; it now generates
into InheritedText for servo with initial value currentcolor, so it
stays inert until authored.

clip-rule, flood-color and lighting-color: FillRule and Color are
already compiled for servo (used by clip-path, fill, stop-color and
others). Nothing downstream consumes them for paint, since SVG filter
primitives aren't implemented.

word-break: break-word: a compat alias (word-break normal plus
overflow-wrap anywhere) with no gecko-only machinery behind it.

font-variant-caps all-small-caps, petite-caps, all-petite-caps, unicase
and titling-caps: mature css-fonts-3 values that map directly to
OpenType feature tags.

background-clip:text and background-attachment:local were
extra_gecko_values, so the servo build rejected them. The background
shorthand drops the whole declaration when any layer keyword fails to
parse, so stylesheets using the gradient-text pattern (background:
linear-gradient(..) plus -webkit-background-clip: text) or scroll
shadows (background-attachment: local) lost their entire background, not
just the modern keyword. Mirror them into extra_servo_values; the
paint-side fallback for clip:text lives in blitz-paint.

The legacy multiline-ellipsis pattern (display:-webkit-box,
-webkit-box-orient:vertical and -webkit-line-clamp:N) needs three
gecko-gated pieces:

- the WebkitBox display variant (with its parse arms, consts and
  FlowRoot const);
- the line-clamp property. Servo gets the line-clamp longhand behind
  layout.css.line-clamp.enabled (like gecko) and the -webkit-line-clamp
  legacy shorthand unconditionally;
- -moz-box-orient (struct xul, generated fresh for servo like the
  fill/InheritedSVG precedent), whose -webkit-box-orient alias carries
  the spelling the web uses.

Also un-gate adjust_for_webkit_line_clamp (the Blink-matching
computed-value rewrite of the clamp trio to flow-root) and set a new
IS_WEBKIT_LINE_CLAMP_CONTEXT flag when it fires. Layout cannot otherwise
tell an adjusted flow-root from an authored one, and the clamp must not
apply to plain blocks that merely set the property.

The remaining parse-only properties:

- css-text: text-wrap-style, hyphens, hyphenate-character,
  hyphenate-limit-chars, text-autospace (and the text-wrap shorthand)
- css-fonts: font-size-adjust, font-palette, font-variant-emoji,
  font-variant-alternates, font-synthesis-{style,small-caps,position}
  (and the font-synthesis shorthand)
- anchor-position: anchor-scope, position-try-order,
  position-visibility (and the position-try shorthand; its
  position-try-fallbacks sub-longhand loses the layout.unimplemented
  servo_pref)
- css-shapes: shape-outside, shape-margin, shape-image-threshold
- text-decor: text-emphasis-{style,position,color},
  text-underline-position, text-decoration-{inset,skip-ink} (and the
  text-emphasis shorthand)
- multicol: column-rule-{style,color,width}, column-fill (and the
  column-rule shorthand)
- contain-intrinsic-{width,height,block-size,inline-size} (and the
  contain-intrinsic-size shorthand)
- others: counter-set, resize, field-sizing, transform-box,
  image-orientation, text-orientation, text-combine-upright,
  scrollbar-gutter

The five handwritten shorthand modules in shorthands.rs were
cfg(gecko)-gated like page-break-*; un-gate them. Servo's font style
struct derives serde, so the newly reachable font value types
(FontPalette, GenericFontSizeAdjust, FontSynthesisStyle,
FontVariantAlternates and VariantAlternates, CustomIdent) gain the same
cfg_attr(servo) serde derives the sibling types carry.

content-visibility stays gecko-gated: its Animate impl is gecko-only,
and whether blitz honours 'hidden' is unverified.

Co-authored-by: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Co-authored-by: Ruskin Constant <ruskin@cloudflare.com>
